{
  "an7.6:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.6 ",
  "an7.6:0.2": "1. Wealth ",
  "an7.6:0.3": "Wealth in Detail ",
  "an7.6:1.1": "“Mendicants, there are these seven kinds of wealth. ",
  "an7.6:1.2": "What seven? ",
  "an7.6:1.3": "The wealth of faith, ethics, conscience, prudence, learning, generosity, and wisdom. ",
  "an7.6:2.1": "And what is the wealth of faith? ",
  "an7.6:2.2": "It’s when a noble disciple has faith in the Realized One’s awakening … ",
  "an7.6:2.3": "",
  "an7.6:2.4": "This is called the wealth of faith. ",
  "an7.6:3.1": "And what is the wealth of ethical conduct? ",
  "an7.6:3.2": "It’s when a noble disciple doesn’t kill living creatures, steal, commit sexual misconduct, use speech that’s false, backbiting, harsh, or nonsensical, or consume intoxicants of beer, wine, and liquor. ",
  "an7.6:3.3": "This is called the wealth of ethical conduct. ",
  "an7.6:4.1": "And what is the wealth of conscience? ",
  "an7.6:4.2": "It’s when a noble disciple has a conscience. They’re conscientious about bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind, and conscientious about having any bad, unskillful qualities. ",
  "an7.6:4.3": "This is called the wealth of conscience. ",
  "an7.6:5.1": "And what is the wealth of prudence? ",
  "an7.6:5.2": "It’s when a noble disciple is prudent. They’re prudent when it comes to bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind, and prudent when it comes to the acquiring of any bad, unskillful qualities. ",
  "an7.6:5.3": "This is called the wealth of prud